<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal &amp; Compliance Framework for IT Notices</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Section 139(9):</strong> Defective return &ndash; 15 days to correct; ITR invalid if not corrected</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 143(1):</strong> CPC intimation within 9 months from FY end; adjustments, demand, or refund</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 143(2):</strong> Scrutiny within 3 months from FY end of filing; assessment under 143(3)</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 142(1):</strong> Inquiry notice &ndash; penalty Rs 10,000 under 271(1)(b)</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 148/148A:</strong> Reassessment &ndash; 3 years normal / 10 years (&gt; Rs 50 lakh or foreign assets)</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 156:</strong> Demand notice &ndash; 30 days to pay; recovery proceedings thereafter</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 154:</strong> Rectification of mistakes apparent from record &ndash; 4 years from order</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 144:</strong> Best judgement assessment if taxpayer fails to respond</li>
                    <li><strong>Section 270A:</strong> Penalty 50% (under-reporting) / 200% (misreporting)</li>
                    <li><strong>ITAT Mumbai:</strong> Income Tax Appellate Tribunal for appeals against assessment orders</li>
                </ul>
                <p><strong>Filing Portal:</strong> <a href="https://www.incometax.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">incometax.gov.in</a> (e-Proceedings module for all responses)</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

