<section id="faq-section" class="content-section" style="background-color: #ffffff;">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="faq-expanded">
                <aside class="faq-expanded__aside">
                    <h2 class="faq-expanded__title">Frequently Asked Questions &ndash; Income Tax Notice in Mumbai</h2>
                    <p class="faq-expanded__lead">Get answers about IT notice types, response deadlines, penalties, AIS mismatches, rectification, and representation for Mumbai taxpayers.</p>
                    @include('partials.faq-enquiry-form', ['enquiryLocation' => 'Mumbai', 'enquiryService' => 'Income Tax Notice in Mumbai'])
                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which IT office handles notices in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>CPC Bengaluru issues Section 143(1) intimations and 139(9) defective return notices. Jurisdictional AOs in Mumbai (based on PAN zone) handle 143(2) scrutiny and 148 reassessment. Commissioner (International Tax) Mumbai handles transfer pricing cases. ITAT Mumbai handles appeals. All responses submitted via e-Proceedings on incometax.gov.in. Patron handles responses for all Mumbai jurisdictions.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What should I do first when I receive an IT notice?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Do not panic. Most notices are routine. First: identify the section number and deadline. Second: download the notice from the e-filing portal. Third: understand what is being asked (correction, information, payment, or appearance). Fourth: gather relevant documents (ITR, Form 16, 26AS, AIS). Fifth: respond within the deadline. For complex notices (143(2) scrutiny, 148 reassessment), engage a CA immediately. Patron provides same-day analysis for Mumbai taxpayers.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is a Section 143(1) intimation?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>An intimation (not scrutiny) from CPC Bengaluru after processing your ITR. It shows income as computed by CPC, tax payable or refund, and any adjustments (TDS corrections, deduction disallowances, AIS income additions). If demand is raised, pay within 30 days or file Section 154 rectification if the adjustment is incorrect. Patron analyses 143(1) intimations and files rectification for incorrect demands.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is Section 148 reassessment?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Issued when the AO believes income has escaped assessment. This is a serious notice. Before issuing 148, the AO sends a Section 148A show-cause notice giving 30 days to explain. If not satisfied, Section 148 is issued requiring a return. Covers 3 years (normal) or 10 years (escaped income &gt; Rs 50 lakh or foreign assets). For Mumbai property sellers and high-value transaction individuals, 148 is the most consequential notice.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the penalty for not responding to an IT notice?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Non-response to 142(1): Rs 10,000 penalty under Section 271(1)(b) plus possible search warrant. Non-response to 143(2): best judgement assessment under Section 144 (AO estimates income, typically unfavourable). Non-correction of 139(9) within 15 days: ITR invalidated. Non-payment of 156 demand within 30 days: recovery proceedings (bank attachment). Under-reporting: 50% penalty; misreporting: 200% under Section 270A.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can I file rectification for an incorrect CPC demand?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. If the 143(1) intimation has errors (wrong TDS credit, incorrect deduction disallowance, computational mistakes), file Section 154 rectification on the e-filing portal. CPC processes rectification in 30-60 days with revised intimation. Common CPC errors for Mumbai: ignoring TDS from job changes, missed HRA exemption, incorrect loss set-off. Patron files rectifications and tracks resolution.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can Patron represent me before the AO?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Patron's CAs hold valid Certificates of Practice and represent with Power of Attorney (Form 26A under IT Rules). Representation includes attending hearings (physical at Mumbai AO office or virtual), making oral and written submissions, producing documents, and negotiating assessments. ITAT Mumbai appeals also handled with professionally drafted grounds and submissions.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>IT notice aaya hai, kya kare?</strong> Pehle section number aur deadline dekho. Portal se notice download karo. 139(9) hai toh 15 din mein correct karo. 143(1) demand hai toh pay karo ya rectification file karo. 143(2) scrutiny hai toh CA se milke documents prepare karo. Patron 24 ghante mein analysis de deta hai.</p>
                <p><strong>Kya notice ignore kar sakte hain?</strong> Bilkul nahi. Har notice ka deadline hota hai. Non-response se: penalty (Rs 10,000+), best judgement assessment (AO khud income estimate karega), recovery proceedings (bank account freeze), aur prosecution ho sakta hai.</p>
                <p><strong>143(1) mein demand aa gaya, kya kare?</strong> Pehle check karo ki demand sahi hai ya CPC ki galti hai. Agar CPC error hai (TDS credit miss, deduction ignore) toh Section 154 rectification file karo online. Agar demand sahi hai toh 30 din mein pay karo.</p>

            </div>
